{"text": "R. DANIEL LAVELLE\n\nCouncilman. City of Pittsburgh-District 6\nChair. Public Satety\n\nSeptember 24, 2019\n\n\u2018The Honorable Stephen Zappala, Esq\nAllegheny County District Attomey\n436 Grant St\nPittsburgh, PA 15219\n\nDistrict Atomey Zappala-\n\n\u2018The images of the violent assault perpetrated by four male employees of the Exxon Mobil gas station in\nMarshall-Shadeland on two African-American women are shocking, disturbing, and an unacceptable display\nof disregard for basic humanity\n\nWhat is equally disturbing to us as Pittsburghers is the anemic legal response from your office in charging\nthree of the four individuals with misdemeanor and simple assault charges. This raises serious questions\nabout equity in our justice system and the disregard of minority communities. If the clear images of two\nAfrican-American women being punched, slammed against a gas pump. and dragged across the pavement,\ndy their hair, are insufficient to warrant more serious charges. it forees one to wonder where the threshold\nlies and may set a dangerous precedent for future incidents\n\nAAs elected representatives in the City of Pittsburgh, we urge your office to elevate the charges leveled\nagainst the men involved in Friday's heinous attack to include, at a minimum, aggravated assault.\n\nverely\n2 Dont Que _ tA WA\n_Gouneigrson R. Danie! Lavelle (Gotpes ts Siete:\n\nAn ay) Viswoyer\n\nConcern Rev. Ricky V. Burgess\n\nAhayte. Kod -Smeth\n\nCouncilperson Anthony Coghill \u2018Councilperson Theresa K. Smith\n\nCouncilperson\n\nCouncilperson Darlene Harris",
